    "cols2_1_3_2_3_2048268876": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-1cc9f530da@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-1cc9f530da@example.invalid",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Jan 24 2024 21:16:50 GMT+0000",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Jan 24 2024 21:16:50 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_1-3_2-3",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-1cc9f530da@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-1f15d09fdf@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Jan 24 2024 21:17:12 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<h2><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Dual-modality HA<sup>+</sup> coating</span></h2>\n<p>The Iconix HA+ coating was designed with HA and bioglass as these materials have been shown to accelerate bone healing at early implantation time.<sup>1,2,3​</sup></p>\n<h2><b><span class=\"fontsize-8em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">Hydroxyapatite + Bioglass</span></span></b></h2>\n<p>Hydroxyapatite is a stable compound shown to be osteoconductive and osteophyllic,<sup>4</sup> with a close structural and chemical resemblance to bone material.<sup>5</sup></p>\n<p>Bioglass is a rapidly dissolving compound with two modes of bioactivity: bone bonding and osteostimulation.<sup>6,7,8&nbsp;</sup></p>\n<p>The Hydroxyapatite and bioglass have been shown in published studies to promote biological fixation between bone and a coated implant.<sup>1,9</sup><br>\n</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Sep 16 2024 17:07:44 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
      "col2": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "standaloneimage": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-1cc9f530da@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-1cc9f530da@example.invalid",
          "preset": "max_width_auto",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Jan 24 2024 21:56:14 GMT+0000",
          "alt": "iconx-ha-plus-magnification",
          "srcFileRef": "/content/dam/stryker/sports-medicine/products/iconix-ha-plus/ha-plus-microscopic-coating-new.png",
          "borderColor": "rgba(76,125,122,1)",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Feb 06 2024 17:02:10 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/standaloneimage",
          "enableBorder": "false"
        }
      }
    },
    "text": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "bottomPadding": "5",
      "jcr:createdBy": "user-1cc9f530da@example.invalid",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-1cc9f530da@example.invalid",
      "hideComponent": "false",
      "jcr:created": "Wed Jan 24 2024 21:19:41 GMT+0000",
      "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
      "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\">Osteostimulatory effect</span></h2>\n<p>Upon implantation, the ionic constituents of bioglass may be released into the surrounding environment and may react with bodily fluids to facilitate the deposition of a thin layer of physiologic calcium phosphate at its surface, thus attracting osteoblasts to the layer to create a matrix that promotes an osteostimulatory effect.<sup>6,7,8,10</sup></p>\n<p>In conjunction, the HA surface may act as a nucleating site for bone minerals,<sup>10,11</sup> thus promoting the adhesion and proliferation of osteoblastic cells on the anchor surface.<sup>1,12</sup><br>\n</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Feb 08 2024 15:06:39 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
    },
